\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 At 24 weeks gestation, fetal magnetoencephalography (fMEG) and, to a lesser extent, fetal EEG (mainly during labor) are the primary tools for directly analysing neural activity. Both can detect increased or abnormal activity, which may signal risk for neurological issues. fMRI and neurosonography provide valuable anatomical context but are less direct for functional assessment{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2881832/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nature.com/articles/pr2000199"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://academic.oup.com/brain/article/147/12/3982/7721052"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}.\
